BSP-Yocto-Ampliphy-AM68x-PD24.1.0                    2024-11-28
===============================================================

- Linux TI vendor kernel v6.1.80 (based on TI tag 09.02.00.009)
  * Tag: v6.1.80-09.02.00.009-phy6
- U-Boot v2023.04 (based on TI tag 09.02.00.009)
  * Tag: v2023.04-09.02.00.009-phy5
- Yocto 4.0.23 (kirkstone)
- QT 5.15

Tested Yocto images:
--------------------

- ampliphy-rauc/phytec-headless-image:
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-2
- ampliphy-xwayland/phytec-qt5demo-image:
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-2
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-3


Build environment:
------------------

- Ubuntu 20.04 64-bit

New features:
-------------

- eMMC HS400 speed mode
- EEPROM based SoM detection to support both 4GB and 8GB ram configurations
- RAUC support
- Watchdog support
- Booting from OSPI Flash
- USB drive support in U-Boot

Issues fixed:
-------------

- The PWM fan is set to 0 when the SoC temperature is exceeding 70° during boot
  time
- The eMMC is limited to HS200 speed mode

Known issues:
-------------

- DFS (Dynamic Frequency Scaling) for the A72 cores is broken and has been
  disabled in the Kernel config.
- Without the SD-Card reset connected some SD-Cards are not detected
  occasionally when booting from other sources.
- As the eMMC reset pin is not connected a power cycle is needed in order to
  reboot using the eMMC boot partitions. (for hw rev 1578.1)
- When booting from the eMMC User Data Area (UDA) an error message is printed
  since the configuration for RAW boot is set too.
- The flashcp command occasionally fails during the verification step.
